# Pairs with RoutingConverges. The undo's last step clears the shadow-forward
# state of the pinned shard only, not of the shard an adaptive split allocated
# above the pinned count (the issue-3880 shape), so k2's shard of T stays in
# Rejecting under the alias that names T again and the tree's own pair is
# refused for k2 forever. Fairness is unchanged; no other operation is
# blocked, so the mutant cannot deadlock instead.
MODULE: RoutingConvergesUndoKeepsFence
TARGET: RoutingConverges
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the undo leaves the split-allocated shard fenced, so the restored tree refuses it forever
PERTURBS: UndoClear

--- FIND
    /\ rz = "undoing"
    /\ alias = T
    /\ fence' = {}
--- REPLACE
    /\ rz = "undoing"
    /\ alias = T
\* MUTATION: only the pinned shard's fence is lifted.
    /\ fence' = fence \ {s1}
--- END